# Bare `node_modules` matches ONLY the context root, so `COPY packages ./packages`
# was dragging the host's packages/*/node_modules into the image — on Windows those
# are pnpm symlinks pointing at C:/Users/..., which dangle under Linux. They landed
# on top of the correct symlinks `pnpm install` had just created, so tsc fell back
# to the hoisted root copy and resolution broke. Every one of these needs `**/`.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.bundle.mjs

.git
.test-postgres

# Secrets never enter the image; they arrive as runtime env (see docker-compose.yml).
# `**/` for the same reason as above — bare `.env.*` matched only the context root,
# so apps/api/.env.dev was being baked in and read at boot inside the container.
**/.env
**/.env.*
docker.env
